#. type: Title #
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:1 docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hub RPC"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Hub RPC** (`HubRPC/1.0`) is the **single business channel** between Hub clients and the agent runtime. Transport:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:11
msgid ""
"**WebSocket** — long-lived connection at **`/hub/rpc/v1`** (connect "
"handshake + heartbeat; HubRPC `req`/`res`/`evt` envelope)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:11
msgid ""
"**HTTP REST** — stateless GET/POST at **`/hub/rpc/v1/{method/path}`** (plain "
"JSON body or query; `Authorization: Bearer`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:13
msgid ""
"Implemented in [`src/shared/hub-rpc/`](../../src/shared/hub-rpc/) (WS "
"envelope + HTTP REST helpers) and [`src/platform/hub/http-rest-router.ts`]"
"(../../src/platform/hub/http-rest-router.ts) (HTTP adapter)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:15
msgid ""
"Binary HTTP methods (e.g. `tts.synthesize`, companion assets, TLS PEM/QR) "
"use Hub RPC REST with registry `request` / `response` encoding. Public "
"probes (`health.probe`, `tls.ca.*`) are Hub RPC methods with `auth: "
"optional` — `GET /hub/rpc/v1/health/probe`, `GET /hub/rpc/v1/tls/ca`, etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:17
msgid ""
"SAP (`SAP/1.0`) is a **session layer** on top of Hub RPC WebSocket: true "
"satellites call `sap.attach` after connect; bundled SPA modules **never** "
"attach."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoints"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ws://{hub_host}:{port}/hub/rpc/v1              # WebSocket upgrade (HubRPC envelope)\n"
"http://{hub_host}:{port}/hub/rpc/v1/task/list  # GET (read-only methods)\n"
"http://{hub_host}:{port}/hub/rpc/v1/task/create # POST (write methods)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:27
msgid ""
"Derive WS URL from HTTP: replace `http` with `ws`, append `/hub/rpc/v1`. "
"Helpers: `resolveHubRpcWsUrl`, `buildHubRestRequest` in `@freeanima/shared/"
"hub-rpc`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:29
msgid ""
"Hub route: [`src/platform/sap/bun-route.ts`](../../src/platform/sap/bun-"
"route.ts)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTTP REST mapping"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:33
msgid ""
"Hub method `domain.action` maps to path **`/hub/rpc/v1/domain/action`** "
"(dots → slashes; camelCase preserved)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:41
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Kind           | HTTP     | Example                                                             |\n"
"| -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Read-only      | **GET**  | `GET /hub/rpc/v1/task/list?subject_kind=user`                       |\n"
"| Write          | **POST** | `POST /hub/rpc/v1/task/create` `{ subject_kind, title, … }`         |\n"
"| By id (read)   | **GET**  | `GET /hub/rpc/v1/task/get/42?subject_kind=user`                     |\n"
"| By id (write)  | **POST** | `POST /hub/rpc/v1/task/patch/42` `{ subject_kind, title?, … }`      |\n"
"| Sensitive read | **POST** | `POST /hub/rpc/v1/vault/get/3` `{ subject_kind, include_secrets? }` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:43
msgid ""
"Route metadata is generated from [`hub-contract`](../../src/shared/hub-"
"contract/) (`meta.http`: `verb`, `path`, `pathParams`). Wrong verb on a "
"known path → **405**; legacy `POST /hub/rpc/v1` envelope → **410**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:45
msgid ""
"HTTP responses are **plain handler JSON** (not HubRPC `res` envelope). "
"Errors: `{ \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\" } }` with 4xx/5xx status."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "WebSocket envelope kinds"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:55
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `kind`      | Direction    | Purpose                                                    |\n"
"| ----------- | ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `connect`   | Client → Hub | WS only: first frame; `protocol: HubRPC/1.0`, `auth_token` |\n"
"| `connected` | Hub → Client | WS only: `session_id`, `heartbeat_interval_sec`            |\n"
"| `req`       | Client → Hub | RPC (`id`, `method`, `payload`)                            |\n"
"| `res`       | Hub → Client | RPC reply                                                  |\n"
"| `evt`       | Both         | Async event (WS only; incl. `heartbeat`)                   |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:57
msgid ""
"HTTP REST uses Bearer on each GET/POST unless the method declares `auth: "
"optional` (e.g. `health.probe`, `tls.ca.*`). WebSocket uses `connect` frame "
"`auth_token` (required)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:59
msgid ""
"Method contracts live in [`src/shared/hub-contract/registry/`](../../src/"
"shared/hub-contract/registry/) (`transports: http | ws`; HTTP routes in "
"`meta.http`). Handlers register via `feature/plugin.hub.rpc`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:63
msgid ""
"Every **WebSocket** connection must send a valid **service API token** in "
"the `connect` payload (`auth_token`). **HTTP REST** uses `Authorization: "
"Bearer fa_at_...` on each request unless the method registry marks `auth: "
"optional` (public read-only probes only). The Hub verifies with "
"`verifyServiceApiToken` ([`src/core/db/pg/service-api-token/`](../../src/"
"core/db/pg/service-api-token/))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:65
msgid ""
"Bundled clients read the token from `window.satelliteShell.remoteAuth.token` "
"(shell bridge), configured in client **Hub settings** (`/settings`). Hub `/"
"web/config.json` does not include tokens."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "Binary HTTP methods"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:69
msgid ""
"Registry `meta.http` may set `request` / `response` encoding (default "
"`json`):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:75
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Encoding             | Use                                                                                                         |\n"
"| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `response: raw`      | Handler returns `Response` (PEM, PNG, VRM, MPEG, octet-stream). Client: `callRaw()` or `fetchHubRestRaw()`. |\n"
"| `request: multipart` | POST with `FormData` body (e.g. `companion.model.upload`).                                                  |\n"
"| `request: raw`       | POST body read from `ctx.httpRequest` in handler.                                                           |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:77
msgid ""
"Examples: `tts.synthesize` (JSON POST → MPEG stream), `companion.asset.get` "
"(GET → VRM), `tls.ca` (GET → PEM)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:79
msgid ""
"Helpers: `hubRestUrl()`, `binaryHttpMeta()` / `rawPublicHttpMeta()` in hub-"
"contract. JSON methods continue to use `hubClient.call()`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "Client profiles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:86
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Profile           | Package entry                                    | `sap.attach` | Typical consumer                               |\n"
"| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Bundled SPA       | `getBundledHubRpcClient()` / `whenHubRpcReady()` | **No**       | Chat, task, notification, diary, email modules |\n"
"| Satellite process | `createSatelliteHub()` in sap-contract           | **Yes**      | companion                                      |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:88
msgid ""
"Bundled SPA shares **one** Hub RPC WebSocket per page load (for streaming, "
"subscriptions, and WS fallback). **`hub-client.call()`** picks transport per "
"method: **read-only** dual-transport methods default to **HTTP GET**; "
"**writes** default to **WebSocket** (`dualTransportMeta` in hub-contract). "
"WS failure on a read-only call falls back to the other channel when "
"`fallback` is enabled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:90
msgid ""
"Satellite processes connect with Hub RPC, then `sap.attach` with `app_id` / "
"`instance_id` before `tool.register` or instance-scoped methods."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <messages><msg>
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:91 docs/sap/transport.md:99 messages/po4a/en.xml:147
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reconnect"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:94
msgid ""
"Use `runHubRpcTransport` for connect, heartbeat, and exponential backoff "
"(default 1s → 30s cap). On satellite detach or socket close, Hub unregisters "
"tools for that instance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/habitat-rpc.md:95
msgid ""
"See also: [transport.md](transport.md) (full state machine), [overview.md]"
"(overview.md)."
msgstr ""
